  "errorLogScreenClearBody": "The entries will disappear from the phone. They can’t be attached to a report afterwards.",
  "featureInfosServerHow": "You can enter two addresses: a remote one (e.g. over Tailscale) and a home one, with the name of your home Wi-Fi network — at home the phone tries the home address first. Recognising the Wi-Fi network needs location permission (an Android rule). “Use current connection” looks for the server on the network by itself. The phone downloads the database from the sources in the order set in Sync › Database (by default the server first, then GitHub). An empty database from the server (0 songs) doesn’t replace the one the phone already has without asking.",
  "featureInfosHomeHow": "Rows from Library (Recently played, Liked Songs, Your playlists, Your moods, Later) and recommendations worked out on the phone from your listening stats and the song database: your most played artists, albums you keep coming back to, new in the database, your genres and Forgotten (songs played at least twice, but not in the last 60 days). You can change the order and visibility of the rows in “Customise home page” (pinning, moving, hiding); the filters at the top narrow the view to songs, playlists or moods.",
  "firstRunScreenAbout": "It’s a public catalogue of songs (titles, artists, albums, moods) from the {repo} repository, downloaded once a day. It makes search, radio, Discover and recommendations work — even without your own MusicDatabase server.",
