  "playbackSettingsScreenMeasureNote": "To level a song, its loudness has to be known. The phone listens once in the background to every song it has whole (files on the phone, downloaded, saved in the cache — the next ones in the queue too) and remembers it. A song heard for the first time without being saved plays unchanged and is measured once it reaches the cache. It takes from a few to about 30 seconds of the phone’s work per song. Off — only files with a stored loudness (ReplayGain tags) are levelled.",
